==French==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|fr|doubter}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{l|fr|doûter}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|fr|la|dubitāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|dubitō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-douter.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{label|fr|followed by the preposition '''[[de]]'''}} to [[doubt]]
#: {{ux|fr|Il ne faut pas '''douter''' de la bonne foi de son interlocuteur.|One must not doubt the intention of their conversational partner.}}
#: {{ux|fr|Je '''doute''' qu'il y parvienne.|I doubt that he will manage.}}
#: {{ux|fr|J'en '''doute'''.|I doubt that.}}
# {{label|fr|reflexive}} to [[suspect]], to have an [[inkling]]
#: {{ux|fr|Je '''me doutais''' qu'il n'allait pas bien, mais je ne savais pas que c'était à ce point-là.|I suspected that he was not doing well, but I did not know that it was to that degree.}}
#: {{ux|fr|Il '''s'en doute''' bien.|He is well aware.}}

====Conjugation====
{{fr-conj-auto}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|fr|douter|Douter}} subordinates a subjunctive content clause when used affirmatively, but subordinates the indicative when used non-affirmatively.
* {{ux|fr|Je doute qu'il '''{{l|fr|avoir|ait}}''' fait ses devoirs.|I doubt that he finished his homework. (positive {{m|fr|douter}}, subjunctive {{m|fr|avoir}})}}
* {{ux|fr|Je ne doute pas qu'il '''{{l|fr|avoir|a}}''' perdu son crayon par accident.|I don't doubt that he lost his pencil by accident. (negative {{m|fr|douter}}, indicative {{m|fr|avoir}})}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fr|à n'en pas douter}}
* {{l|fr|ne douter de rien}}

